    <string name="appsettings_encryption_info_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="appsettings_encryption_info_message">The app database is encrypted locally with AES-256 (SQLCipher). The key is generated randomly and wrapped with a hardware key in the Android Keystore (StrongBox if available, otherwise the device\'s secure processor) – it never leaves the keystore unencrypted.\n\nOnce encryption is on, new Google Drive and local backups are encrypted with the same key from then on, additionally recoverable with your backup password. Backups that already existed before are not encrypted retroactively – they stay as they are until replaced by a new backup.</string>
    <string name="appsettings_encryption_backup_nag_title">Encryption without a backup</string>
    <string name="appsettings_encryption_backup_nag_message">Your database is encrypted, but no backup exists yet. If the encryption key is lost (e.g. device change, repair, or factory reset), all data is gone permanently.</string>
